      "id": "xhfo2qr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Energy is defined as the capacity or ability to do work, and its SI unit is the Joule (J).",
        "Kinetic Energy (KE = 1/2 * m * v²) is the energy possessed by an object due to its state of motion.",
        "Potential Energy (PE = m * g * h) is the stored energy an object possesses due to its position or configuration.",
        "The Law of Conservation of Energy states that energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed from one form to another.",
        "Mechanical Energy is the sum total of kinetic energy and potential energy in a closed system.",
        "Power is defined as the rate of doing work or the rate of energy consumption per unit time (P = Work / Time)."
      ],
      "id": "z8qizdh"
    },
